    "constants_widths_signedness_pointer_arithmetic": {
      "target_model": "MSC 6.00AX large model: int and unsigned int are 16-bit; long is signed 32-bit; plain char is signed 8-bit; far pointers are 16:16.",
      "record_layout": "off starts at signed-long 4. Every record has a 4-byte tag header. P payload=12 bytes plus 10 bytes per signed nLinks; T payload=10 bytes plus 2 bytes per signed nFrames. Tags are 0x50 and 0x54. Unknown tags set off=size.",
      "byte_order": "FlipWords swaps adjacent bytes for a signed-long length (calls use 12,10,10,2 and hStyl byte size). XFlipLong swaps the two words in each 20-byte StyleRun.pos after style word-byte conversion.",
      "comparisons": "off<size and off<tlen-4 are signed-long comparisons using signed high and unsigned low words. Link/frame/style loops use signed 16-bit int. StyleRun.pos>=off is signed long. *q<space is signed char.",
      "pointer_rules": "base+off reads far data using base.segment and base.offset+low16(off) modulo 65536; target operations preserve segment. nul-text and q-nul are same-segment signed 16-bit differences sign-extended for off/style arithmetic. tlen narrows long resource size to signed int; memory-helper lengths convert to unsigned int.",
      "coordinate_math": "Rect and record fields are signed 16-bit ints; bitmap coordinates and text-rect translation add with 16-bit wrap. Constants: title object 0x501, window 0x502, clip window 0x500, resource kinds 0x11/0x13/10/0x15, type 1, fonts 2 and 5, record flag 1, control limit 0x20, reserved tail 4."
    },
